-- statement:
--   Direct evaluation of `T⁻¹_{uv}` (any `u, v < n`).
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.J6SegEnt`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem J6Seg.TinvD_err {T : Tables} {a n : ℕ} {E : ℝ} (hα : 2 ≤ α) (hσ : 1 ≤ σ)
--       (hx : 2 ≤ α ^ 2 * (σ - 1)) (hb : |b| ≤ 1 / 2) (hT : BlkTab P α σ b T a n E) (hE : 0 ≤ E)
--       (hP : 100 * (((n : ℝ) + 1) * E + 1) ≤ 2 ^ P) {u v : ℕ} (hu : u < n) (hv : v < n) :
--       |(fmul P (fmul P (T.gi u) (T.gi v)) (TsumI P T a n u v) : ℝ) / 2 ^ P -
--         TinvF α σ b n u v| ≤ 7 * (((n : ℝ) + 1) * E + 1) / 2 ^ P
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** Segmented inverse (S2): single entries of the block inverse (capacitance corners)
--
--   `TinvI` evaluates `T⁻¹_{uv}` directly or through persymmetry (`TinvF_persym`), `MinvI`
--   evaluates `M⁻¹_{uv} = D_u T⁻¹_{uv} D_v⁻¹`.  With `K = (n+1)E + 1`, `100 K ≤ 2^P`:
--   `|TinvI/2^P - T⁻¹_{uv}| ≤ 7K/2^P` and `|MinvI/2^P - M⁻¹_{uv}| ≤ 12 Dm K/2^P`.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** Part of the Lean formalization of the round-six κ-improvement (integer-multiplication-kappa campaign, target `IntMul.Kappa.jain_round6_framework`). The statement is copied verbatim from the Lean development; the platform node carries the same declaration name. Definitions it mentions live in the `IntMul_Kappa_R6_Defs*` bundles (on top of the published κ bundles `IntMul_Kappa_K_Defs*`).
